"""Walk-through of lesson 35, Testing.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script): a basket of 3 items at 9.99 with a 10% code: 29.97, 10% off = 2.997, total 26.973 -> 26.97.
The bug rounds the discount down to 2.99 first: 26.98, one cent too much; on 10,000 orders = 100.00.
5,000 unit tests x 2 ms = 10 s; 300 integration tests x 2 s = 600 s = 10 min; 20 contract tests x 3 s = 60 s; 8 end-to-end tests x 3 min = 24 min.
In all 10 + 600 + 60 + 1,440 = 2,110 s = about 35 min over 5,328 tests. Upside down: 500 end-to-end x 3 min = 1,500 min = 25 h.
Flaky: 1 run in 20 fails; 20 such tests leave a run green 0.95^20 = 36% of the time. Load test: knee at 800/s against a busiest day of 400/s (2x).
"""
